	"descriptionMarkdown": "\nInput\n- 95.7 / min Yumako\n- 38.3 / min Jellynut\n- Water (stable supply)\n\n\nOutput\n- 143 Agricultural science pack / min\n\nStartup Procedure (order matters)\nTo start infinite stable production:\n1. Start Yumako and Jellynut belts.\n2. Insert into the top biochamber (Nutrients from Bioflux): minimum 15 Bioflux, minimum 9 Nutrients\n3. Insert minimum 2 Pentapod eggs into each egg-producing biochamber.\n\nThree manual items required:\n- Bioflux\n- Nutrients\n- Pentapod eggs\nAfter this, the system becomes fully self-sustaining.\n\nStability Conditions\n\nTo prevent failure:\n1. Seed chests must always have free space.\n2. The Agricultural science pack chest must always have free space.\n3. Fruit supply must be continuous.\nIf these conditions are met, production runs indefinitely.\n\nDesign Properties\n- No spoilage.\n- No circuit logic.\n- Fully deterministic throughput.\n- Clean, readable, modular layout.\n\n\nScaling\n\nTo double production:\n1. Place an identical module next to it.\n2. Connect the same inputs.\n3. Merge outputs.\nLinear scaling. No cross-module dependencies.\n",
